    id: 'reading-b1-radio', domain: 'reading', targetLevel: 'B1', type: 'personal_account',
    title: 'My first month at community radio',
    text: 'When I joined the community radio station, I imagined myself interviewing musicians. I had listened to the Saturday music programme for years and thought I knew how it worked. On my first evening, however, the producer asked me to check the names and times in a list of local events. I went home disappointed. It seemed a long way from the conversations I wanted to have on air.\n\nA week later, an organiser called to say that we had announced the wrong entrance for her concert. I found the mistake in a message she had sent us: the information had changed, but nobody had updated the list. The producer asked me to call her back, check the details and record a short correction. It was my first time speaking on the programme.\n\nSince then, I have started phoning organisers before we announce their events. These calls often turn into interesting conversations. One man explained why he had started a walking group for people who were new to the town, and we invited him into the studio. I still want to interview musicians, but I no longer see checking information as a job that keeps me away from the interesting work. Sometimes it is how that work begins.',
