    title: 'Two messages about the shared kitchen',
    text: 'Message from Priya to the residents’ group\n\nSeveral people have asked whether we should replace the sign-up sheet for our shared kitchen with an online calendar. I support trying this. The sheet is inside the building, so people often make a special journey just to discover that the time they want has already been booked. An online calendar would let us check before setting out. It would also make it easier to see who to contact if we wanted to exchange a booking.\n\nI am not suggesting that everybody must book online. We could leave a phone number on the kitchen door and have a volunteer enter bookings for anyone who prefers to call. My main concern is that two separate calendars would soon disagree. If we try this, the online record needs to contain every booking, however it was made.\n\nReply from Mark\n\nThe unnecessary journeys are a real problem, and I agree that one complete record would be better than two incomplete ones. What worries me is the arrangement for entering telephone bookings. It sounds simple while one enthusiastic volunteer is doing it. But what happens when that person is away, or when a call comes in just before an online booking for the same time?\n\nBefore choosing a calendar, I would like us to agree who responds to calls, how quickly they do it, and what we tell someone while a request is waiting to be entered. Once that is clear, I would be happy to support a four-week trial. During the trial, we should record failed or delayed bookings as well as successful ones; otherwise, a tidy calendar may give us a misleading picture of how well the arrangement works.',
    source: 'original', clusterId: 'reading-b2-kitchen',
